From 754f35cee245c0c9965a7bb827c07d18fd5c3a06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:35:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/28] builds: the cost note says where the last build of each
 kind ran

The form's cost note quoted GitHub's prices for every build, including Mac
builds that run on a Mac of your own and cost nothing: confusing. rdgen
cannot read the repository variables that route jobs (its runtime token has
Actions access only), but it can see where jobs ran.

- When a run completes, the poller lists its jobs (before deleting a
  successful run) and records each job's runner, and whether it was one of
  GitHub's machines (runner group "GitHub Actions"): GithubRun.runners,
  migration 0007.
- The form gets, per kind of build (Windows, Windows 32-bit, Linux, Intel
  Mac, Apple Silicon Mac, and the small setup/bridge/cleanup jobs), where the
  last completed one ran. The note then says "your own Mac (runner) built it
  last time, so no GitHub Actions minutes", or GitHub's cost where it ran on
  GitHub's machines or nothing is known yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
